I found a concrete risk in the parallel worker path: cut-edge messages are being deduplicated by payload signature, which can suppress legitimate repeated transfers when the same value crosses the same partition boundary twice. I’m checking whether I can reproduce that case with a small graph, then I’ll patch that logic directly if it holds up.
